# dsv41: KV sharding in the lanes (port of GLM 0118, second half,
# MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#152): 0015's planner (parts.zig) runs placement, release,
# verify and the follower, so every extent lives inside one part and the pair serves --parallel streams. A cache hit
# whose part has no room is carried to the other part (its latents sent by the owner) only when that saves a
# recompute, an eviction or a pause, never to even out the parts
# (TF_DS_KV_SHARD_CARRY=1); a prompt that runs from 0 borrows free rows of the other part and attends locally instead
# of fetching (TF_DS_KV_SHARD_TWINS=1; the borrowed rows go back at its first decode round). kv_lanes.zig: rank 0's Kv
# (plan, apply, send, run and finish each transfer over 0016's rank_wire) and the follower (replay, transfers, binds,
# round checks); the ranks compare the planner's digest every TF_DS_KV_SHARD_CHECK decode rounds (1024; 0: at start
# only). core/lanes/kv_parts.zig: the parts' stats, on /health kv_shard and /metrics.
# Switches (both ranks; in the startup agreement's features): TF_DS_KV_SHARD_CARRY 1, TF_DS_KV_SHARD_TWINS 1,
# TF_DS_KV_SHARD_CHECK 1024, all inert unless TF_DS_KV_SHARD=1 (then a pool of at least two windows, e.g. 2,101,248
# for the 1M window; the recipe's KV_SHARD derives it when POOL is empty). Off: Lanes.kv stays null and every frame,
# placement and byte is as before.
# Measured on the pair (engine 98370ef, before the rebase onto 0008; pool 2,101,248, 8 streams): exact.py 31/31
# identical to the daily baseline with carries and borrowing off (kept rows in both parts, 167,936 and 118,784, so
# rank 1 owned conversations) and with the defaults (24 borrowed extents; prompt fetches 3,774 -> 304, prompt bytes
# 13.9 GB -> 0.42 GB). Decode at this stage runs NCCL collectives each compressed layer: -10.6 % at one stream, -12.3 %
# at eight; 0022 moves the exchange onto the RDMA ring. Builds on 0015 and 0016. By Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
# Apache-2.0.
